## Repair r1

Same author (`claude-opus-5-5`), same session, 2026-10-10, from `REPAIR-BRIEF.md`, `source-tracking.md` and both reviews. All edits were composed by hand, by reading; replacements were written as exact-string edits or whole-scene redrafts. No script split or joined sentences. No git command was run. `protected-patterns.txt` was not touched. The pre-repair text is in `pre-repair/`.

### Rulings applied

- **Seln:** not told (the coordinator confirms source Ch15 = edition M6). Nothing changed.
- **The day-45 Velmere letter is SEALED** (ch16): Brom turns it over once, puts it unopened in the left inside pocket; nobody asks; his hand returns to the pocket. It is carried visibly through ch18 (in his coat on the frame), ch19 (his hand on the pocket on the stair; "four days ago… unopened"), and ch20 (left pocket "had a sealed letter in it"). It is the letter BOOK_MAP §4e #10 carries to M7.
- Calendar, the third-sitting set-aside, the new canon (gallery, chain, small burst, fee office, road column, lane shadow), the level and the honest floor: kept as accepted.

### Method (P1 order)

1. `EVENT-LIST.md` was rewritten first: every scene the source-distance read found tracked now has a new way in and a new order of beats, worked out in my words with the source closed (the r1 note at its head).
2. Whole redrafts from that list: **ch14**, **ch19**, **ch20 scenes 2–6**. Scene 1 of ch20 (the honest floor) is unchanged.
3. Scene-level re-composition of **ch15–18**. In practice I redrafted the tracked scenes whole rather than line by line, because a passage-by-passage pass kept the old order: ch15 scenes 2–4, ch16 whole, ch17 scenes 3–4, ch18 scene 1 and the tracked passages of scenes 2–3.

