     1	# Chapter 19 — The Shape
     2	
     3	When the plates had been cleared, Seln put four dried beans on the board in a row and said, "Four offices. Ask."
     4	
     5	They were the speckled brown beans the kitchen soaked for the Second-day stew. He had taken them out of his coat pocket without any hurry and laid them a hand's breadth apart, in front of his own place at the middle of the bench, and now he sat back from them with his hands folded and looked at none of the four people across the table.
     6	
     7	Nobody asked anything for a moment. The refectory went on round them, loud at the far end where the first-years were.
     8	
     9	"A drawing can be found," said Seln, to the beans. "These can be eaten. Ask."
    10	
