idn't fail this time?"; Lira leaves without the "Bed" line; Brom's second "Corridor." comes at the door.</li><li>Pole frame: "The entry was finished before the pen touched paper."</li><li>The prolepsis is trimmed to "It looked like the truth, because, as far as he could see from that window, it was."</li><li>The lamps go out by the hall's own count (the counter pair, the table's pairs from the far end, the press lamp last).</li></ul> |
