editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:154:- **Cael:** fit. Rested the hip on d30 by Rooke's order, after four bursts on the second floor's boards (worth five there). A stung left forearm from Ephram's lath (d29), a day's matter. The right shoulder is unused. Shadow rent runs from waking; drifts are in the gaps only; one in the last recess week. Zero deployment anywhere.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:155:- **Lira, Brom, Ephram:** fit. Ordinary floor knocks from the mock bouts. Brom's right fist is strapped from habit, healed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:163:- New learned technique, not a fragment: **the heel correction against the second-year entry**, about one in three, then two in three, with the plain-entry mix still unsolved. Plus reading Ephram's shoulder drop. Both are skill, not capability.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:166:- **Cael** knows the Standard's architecture (marks, strikes, par thirty, the bands, weighting, exhibitions rated for the figure only). He has priced Lira, Brom and Ephram correctly ahead of the panel. He knows the abbreviation on the card and that some unseen hand let the advisory go through; he does not know Vastin wrote it. He saw Karis mark a page in Rooke's manual (he does not know which), and he saw her write a note in the founding articles (he does not know what).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:169:- **Vastin** knows the advisory, the routing slip's unknown initials, and that the roster stands. He has no knowledge of fragments and no suspicion of Seln.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:178:- Gault's case with the handle.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:183:- **Ephram:** "from rival to colleague" moves to trade partners (heel for shoulders). He takes the rating and minds losing the bout.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:188:- **Gault:** marks what the manual says.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:198:  - The routing slip's two letters (Vastin, private).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:200:- Closed: the roster question (printed); Ephram's "next term" sheet (signed d5).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:207:- (e) Vastin's room is not the source's "western administration, third floor, river side". It is a high room in the Compact's house with a court and pigeons. No location is named.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:208:- (f) Gault's next evaluation is called "the provision's second" (per §12 C8 / N4).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:220:- **Gault's case (flag, minor):** dark oak, brass corners. The saddler-stitched handle was sent by the frame-maker. Gault has written him three drafts of a letter.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:222:- **The second-year entry (flag, technique):** two weights, the front honest and the back heel held; the correction is "wait for the heel" at the cost of the first share; the plain entry is mixed in; Ephram's shoulders drop on full commitment (since corrected). Rooke's boards: *Wait for the heel. Cost: the first share. Fine.* · *Enrollee: heel, one in three, nearer two. Ephram: shoulders. Good trade.* · *Better. Both.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:223:- **Ephram's supervised sessions:** the sheet was signed on d5. Two a week at the second bell with Rooke at the rail; held d12 and d17.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:233:- **Vastin's room and routing slip (flag):**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:247:  - Panel: Gault, Karis, Rooke and the two reserves, with Rooke's own examiner's manual (his cycle's; the annotated one remains M2's).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:248:  - Ratings: Ephram 23.66, Cael 23.00 (8 / 8.66 / 6.33), Lira 26.33, Brom 23.66. Cael won 2–1; Lira won 2–1 in the fourth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:250:- **Pine floors at the wool town (flag, M2 terrain):** they give on the left side of the main hall, by the old wall (via Ephram's cousin's house).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:263:- Titles: Lira and Brom two each across the two meets (Brom unbeaten: 'bouts unbeaten, none lost'); Ephram's first regional final; Karis third in a 'three-exchange family argument'. Page thirty-one via Bracken's 'front third' pays Karis's ch6 strip. The movement ends on the first pole (protected item 21) at the coaching inn: 'Not this season's problem.' Year counts not incremented. Cael's mock-ring ratings: once (23.00); rated three times by ch11.
