editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-14.md:205:"The quarry town," he said. "Ten days by the hill roads, and the post up there is a matter of faith." He laid the page on its pile. "So I'll send a pouch after you. The records office keeps one for the hill coach, which goes up on the Second-day and the Sixth-day, and it will find you at the quarry town if the hill coach finds the quarry town, which it generally does."
