editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-15.md:71:*The proceedings' evaluation seat is fully constituted. Supplementary findings are not contemplated by the schedule.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-15.md:123:"I'll say this standing," she said, "so nobody takes it for advice. Don't let tonight make him yours. The Archmarshal is the Compact's officer. He asked a Compact seat under the Compact's code, and the Compact told him no, and every part of that is one house talking to itself." She drew her right glove tighter. "What I can give you is only the shape of the no. I have been refused a great many times in twenty-six years. I've been refused with no citation at all perhaps five times, and each of the five was an office that had made up its mind already and did not want its reasons where somebody could read them later. Keep every citation they give you. Keep a note of each one they don't." She turned on the stair. "Its absence is a finding."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-15.md:135:"They benched their best instrument because he measures true."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-18.md:27:*I fought him. Your instruments failed him, not the other way around. Classify the instruments.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-18.md:109:*They did this to me the other way — built the ladder to my height and called it fairness. Nobody files challenges against a favorite. Don't mistake what's happening to you for procedure. It stopped being procedure the day they couldn't score you.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-14.md:139:*The proceedings' evaluation seat is fully constituted. Supplementary findings are not contemplated by the schedule.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-14.md:185:*Pending a proceeding worth sending it to.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-19.md:79:*Two polite men from the registry came through Denvash asking after my trade licenses and the shop's title. Wanted to know if you had any interest recorded in either. I told them my grandson's interest in this shop is that he grew up in it, and they wrote that down. Whatever they're building, it has a shape. Mind the shape. — H.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-19.md:131:"For a smith with a forge and a wife and a guild, six weeks. Ten, if the wife's people are spread about." He looked at the four in their row and the one apart. "For a boy with friends at three provincial registries, and a house that took him in, and a grandfather with a shop at the far end of the country—" He laid one finger flat on the board beside the fifth bean. "Nine weeks. They are in the sixth."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-19.md:145:"There are men in Denvash asking an old man about a tin box," she said, evenly, the way she read the true sum off a bout sheet after a loss. "And we're down here being good at sittings. We are good at them. Karis wrote the best thing anybody's ever written on this hill, and the house's counsel wins whatever there is to win, and the seat writes it all down." She put the bean back exactly where it had been. "They'll let us be good at sittings all year. It costs them nothing." Her chin came up. "The question is what we do the day after."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-19.md:197:"Takes exactly as long as somebody would like it to," said Withrow. "That's the whole design. Not a hand on the door. A hand on the clock."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-20.md:91:*I fought him. Your instruments failed him, not the other way around. Classify the instruments.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-20.md:279:"We won every point that can be won on paper."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-20.md:283:"And it's proceeding."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-20.md:291:*Part of me is still keeping score. The rest of me has started counting doors.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-20.md:295:"Now you understand the file I've been reading my whole career."

